_np = [['Compare three models, such as a single brand, several brands from one kitchen or a shared kitchen, using set-up cost, volume needed and staffing for each.', 'Estimate the weekly orders needed to break even, for example 120 orders at an average 14 with a 30 percent food cost, before you commit.'], ['Choose dishes that travel well for 30 minutes, test each in a closed box, and drop any that turn soggy, cold or separated on arrival.', 'Keep the menu to 12 to 15 items using shared ingredients, so waste falls and the kitchen can prepare orders faster.'], ['Check what permits, registrations and inspections your area requires before renting any space, and keep copies of every document in one folder.', 'Plan a layout with separate zones for raw food, cooked food and packing, with a hand-wash sink and clear cleaning schedule.'], ['Write a simple food safety plan that lists each step from delivery to hand-over, the temperature or time limit, and who checks it.', 'Record fridge and hot-holding temperatures twice daily on a sheet, label all stored food with a prepare-by date, and act at once on any reading outside the limit.'], ['Cost each dish by adding ingredients, packaging and a share of platform fees, then set prices so the food cost stays near 30 percent.', 'Compare your price with similar nearby kitchens and test one small increase, watching whether order numbers change over two weeks.'], ['Set a prep time per dish, for instance 12 minutes, and cap incoming orders per quarter-hour so the kitchen is never overloaded.', 'Time the full cycle from order to hand-off, and review late orders weekly to find whether prep, packing or pickup causes the delay.'], ['Create a clear name, logo and short description, and use real, well-lit photos of the packed meal that customers will actually receive.', 'Reply to every review within a day, thank positive ones, and log complaints to see which dish or step is causing repeat problems.'], ['Review weekly sales by dish, waste in kilograms and refunds, and remove the weakest two menu items each month.', 'Scale only when you can keep quality on time for four weeks in a row, then add hours, a second brand or a new area.']]
